# seed: 1
# requires: boot_menu hero_ready map_enter path_found hero_move
# Option 7, "Enable automatic Way Point calculations", gates the pathfinder and is OFF in
# retail (DAT_006840D0 is all-zero at boot -- see src/game/options.c), so this replay has to
# TICK IT, the way a player does: open the Options dialog and set the checkbox, via the .dsc
# `dialog` op. There is no pre-boot shortcut, because the original has none.
# Evergreen spawn (179,202); click (226,192) targets map (190,198). The direct line hits
# the shoreline, so the original's pathfinder walks the wall: it retries up to 10 times
# (FUN_004620F3's gate) picking the first unblocked neighbour each try. So this asserts
# that a path was FOUND and that the hero ARRIVED, not a node count or a node order --
# those are implementation details the 10-try walk does not fix.
expect boot_menu 900
key RETURN
wait 30
key RETURN
wait 30
# Three states before the Well, not two: 1 main menu -> 2 the
# "Where Do You Want To Play Today?" splash (FUN_0041D31F) -> 3 the world
# list (FUN_0041D717). The original's own table is FUN_0041B891 (all.c:21078);
# the port used to collapse the splash, so the script had drifted. The extra
# RETURN is the plan's keyboard shortcut for the row click (msg 0x474).
key RETURN
wait 30
key n
wait 5
text PathWalker
key RETURN
expect hero_ready 300
expect map_enter 600
click 226 192
expect path_found 120
expect hero_move 600
quit
